  <h2>Is Airhub or Holafly the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Airhub if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You know roughly how many GB you'll use and want the lowest price per gigabyte</li>
        <li>You want SMS and a local number bundled with your data, not sold as an extra</li>
        <li>You're headed somewhere Airhub prices sharply, like Thailand or Japan</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with Holafly if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You genuinely don't know how much data you'll use</li>
        <li>Heavy streaming, video calls, or hotspot use</li>
        <li>China is on the itinerary and you want the built-in VPN</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Airhub still doesn't replace a real phone number.</strong> It bundles SMS and, on most plans, a local number, but there's no voice calling, so it's not a full substitute if you need to actually receive or make calls abroad. If a real number with calls guaranteed matters, <a href="/simlocal/">SimLocal</a>'s UK plans include one.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Neither "unlimited" is truly unmanaged.</strong> Holafly's unlimited plans can apply a fair-use speed reduction after very heavy same-day use, though it isn't published as a specific daily GB number. Airhub has no such issue since you're buying a fixed block to begin with: you simply run out of what you bought.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Airhub vs Holafly FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Airhub or Holafly</h3>
      <p>Airhub, for most trips, since you're paying a low per-GB block price instead of a flat daily unlimited rate. Holafly only wins on price (or at least on predictability) if you'd otherwise burn through multiple Airhub blocks in a single day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does Airhub include a phone number like a real SIM</h3>
      <p>On most plans, yes, a local number plus SMS, but not voice calls. It covers receiving a verification text or giving out a temporary number, not making or taking phone calls.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which one is better for a trip to China</h3>
      <p>Holafly, if you don't want to set up a separate VPN: its China eSIM includes one built in. Airhub has no equivalent for China.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I just buy whichever is cheapest for my specific destination</h3>
      <p>That works for a single short trip. For longer or heavier-use trips, run the math on expected GB per day against Airhub's block pricing before assuming it's the cheaper option; past a certain point Holafly's flat rate overtakes it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

